# Lint — Biome and Tailwind CSS

After every code change, check Biome **and** Tailwind CSS diagnostics, then apply the fixes. Do not leave warnings.

- **Biome:** run `pnpm check` and read editor diagnostics. `src/styles.css` is excluded from Biome — still lint it via Tailwind.
- **Tailwind IntelliSense:** fix `suggestCanonicalClasses` and `cssConflict`, plus `invalidApply` / `invalidScreen` / similar issues.

```tsx
// ❌ cssConflict — both set min-height; last class wins
<div className="min-h-dvh min-h-svh" />

// ✅ one utility
<div className="min-h-dvh" />

// ❌ non-canonical
<div className="absolute end-0 has-[:focus-visible]:ring-3" />

// ✅ canonical
<div className="absolute inset-e-0 has-focus-visible:ring-3" />
```
